In article <2jtj00$nbk@rc1.vub.ac.be>, hw41652@is2e.vub.ac.be (Van Deun Dirk) writes:
>
>Teleport+teleport control are very handy for quick escapes, but it's
>very annoying that NH keeps trying to random-teleport you when you have
>teleport control, so that you have to hit ESC twice every +-50 (?)
>moves. IMNSHO, NH should stop doing that, because it has no effect but
>annoying the player. The random teleports should only be there if you
>_cannot_ control them. (= when you have no teleport control, or when you
>are asleep/unconscious)
>
No, no! There's one important point: random teleports don't make you hungry.
This way you can speed up your progress through mapped levels immensely - just
start moving in the right direction, and when the game asks about the teleport
- show on your destination... And this does not cost you anything - using
^T costs power and food...

Remember: there is something useful in almost every annoying feature of
this game :-)

